The fix is confirmed. The `invalidateCache()` method now properly clears the cache:

```typescript
private invalidateCache(): void {
    this.cacheValid = false;
    this.statusCache = null;
}
```

This ensures that after any task mutation (create, update, delete), the next call to `filterByStatus()` will recompute the results from the actual task data instead of returning stale cached results.

